{
  "id": "p13",
  "title": "Enumerations and Ranges",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "p13-l1",
      "title": "Your Own Values",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Pascal lets you invent your own types. An enumeration lists all its values: type TColor = (red, yellow, green); A variable of that type can only hold one of them.",
        "That's clearer than numbers: light := green; says what it means, and light := 7; is an error the compiler catches.",
        "Enumeration values can be compared, used in case, and looped over. But Turbo Pascal can't writeln them directly: you need an array of names."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Light;",
          "type",
          "  TColor = (red, yellow, green);",
          "var",
          "  light: TColor;",
          "begin",
          "  light := red;",
          "  if light = red then",
          "    writeln('Stop!');",
          "  case light of",
          "    red: writeln('red');",
          "    yellow: writeln('yellow');",
          "    green: writeln('green');",
          "  end;",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": []
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p13-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is an enumeration type?",
          "options": [
            "A type that lists all its possible values",
            "A list of numbers",
            "An array",
            "A string"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "type TDay = (mon, tue, wed, thu, fri, sat, sun);"
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why is light := green better than light := 3?",
          "options": [
            "It says what it means, and wrong values are caught",
            "It's faster",
            "It uses less memory",
            "It isn't"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Readable code, and the compiler checks it."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l1-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Declare an enumeration.",
          "code": [
            "type",
            "  TSuit = (hearts, diamonds, clubs___ spades);"
          ],
          "options": [
            ",",
            ";",
            "..",
            "|"
          ],
          "answer": ",",
          "explanation": "The values are separated by commas, in round brackets."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l1-e4",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program doesn't compile. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "program Days;",
            "type",
            "  TDay = (mon, tue, wed);",
            "var",
            "  d: TDay;",
            "begin",
            "  d := tue;",
            "  writeln(d);",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 7,
          "explanation": "Turbo Pascal can't write enumeration values: Error 64. Use case or an array of names."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l1-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program L;",
            "type",
            "  TColor = (red, yellow, green);",
            "var",
            "  light: TColor;",
            "begin",
            "  light := green;",
            "  case light of",
            "    red: writeln('stop');",
            "    yellow: writeln('wait');",
            "    green: writeln('go');",
            "  end;",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "go",
            "stop",
            "wait",
            "nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "light is green."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l1-e6",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program doesn't compile. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "program Col;",
            "type",
            "  TColor = (red, green, blue);",
            "var",
            "  c: TColor;",
            "begin",
            "  c := 2;",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 6,
          "explanation": "c can only hold red, green or blue, not a number: Error 26: Type mismatch."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p13-l2",
      "title": "ord, succ and pred",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Enumeration values are counted from 0: ord(red) is 0, ord(yellow) 1, ord(green) 2.",
        "succ(x) is the next value, pred(x) the one before. succ of the last value is an error.",
        "A for loop can run over an enumeration: for d := mon to fri do … And arrays can use it as index: names: array[TColor] of string."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Week;",
          "type",
          "  TDay = (mon, tue, wed, thu, fri, sat, sun);",
          "const",
          "  dayName: array[TDay] of string = ('Mon', 'Tue', 'Wed', 'Thu', 'Fri', 'Sat', 'Sun');",
          "var",
          "  d: TDay;",
          "begin",
          "  for d := mon to sun do",
          "    write(dayName[d], ' ');",
          "  writeln;",
          "  d := wed;",
          "  writeln('After ', dayName[d], ' comes ', dayName[succ(d)], ', number ', ord(succ(d)));",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": []
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p13-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "If type TSize = (small, medium, large), what is ord(large)?",
          "options": [
            "2",
            "3",
            "1",
            "0"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Counting starts at 0."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is succ(small)?",
          "options": [
            "medium",
            "large",
            "1",
            "small"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The next value in the list."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l2-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What happens with succ(large) when large is the last value?",
          "options": [
            "Runtime error 201: Range check error",
            "It wraps to small",
            "It gives large",
            "Nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "There is no value after the last one."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l2-e4",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Give every color a name to print.",
          "code": [
            "  names: array[___] of string = ('red', 'green', 'blue');"
          ],
          "options": [
            "TColor",
            "1..3",
            "string",
            "0..2"
          ],
          "answer": "TColor",
          "explanation": "The enumeration itself can be the index type."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l2-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program W;",
            "type",
            "  TDay = (mon, tue, wed, thu, fri);",
            "const",
            "  n: array[TDay] of string = ('Mon', 'Tue', 'Wed', 'Thu', 'Fri');",
            "var",
            "  d: TDay;",
            "begin",
            "  for d := tue to thu do",
            "    write(n[d], ' ');",
            "  writeln;",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "Tue Wed Thu",
            "Mon Tue Wed",
            "1 2 3",
            "an error"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The loop goes from tue to thu."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l2-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Can enumeration values be compared, like mon < fri?",
          "options": [
            "Yes, by their order in the list",
            "No, never",
            "Only with =",
            "Only in case"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "mon comes first, so mon < fri is true."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p13-l3",
      "title": "Subranges",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A subrange is a part of another type: var month: 1..12; or var grade: 'A'..'F'; It works like the bigger type, but only allows those values.",
        "Storing a value outside the range stops the program with Runtime error 201: Range check error. That finds mistakes early.",
        "Subranges are also handy as array indexes: type TMonth = 1..12; days: array[TMonth] of integer."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Months;",
          "type",
          "  TMonth = 1..12;",
          "const",
          "  days: array[TMonth] of integer = (31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31);",
          "var",
          "  month: TMonth;",
          "begin",
          "  month := 2;",
          "  writeln('Month ', month, ' has ', days[month], ' days');",
          "  month := month + 10;",
          "  writeln('Month ', month);",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": []
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p13-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What can var hour: 0..23; hold?",
          "options": [
            "The whole numbers from 0 to 23",
            "Any integer",
            "Only 0 and 23",
            "Reals from 0 to 23"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "A subrange of integer."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What happens when hour := 24; runs?",
          "options": [
            "Runtime error 201: Range check error",
            "hour becomes 0",
            "hour becomes 23",
            "Nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "24 is outside 0..23."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l3-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Allow only the small letters.",
          "code": [
            "var",
            "  letter: 'a'___'z';"
          ],
          "options": [
            "..",
            ",",
            "-",
            " to "
          ],
          "answer": "..",
          "explanation": "A range of chars works just like a range of numbers."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l3-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program S;",
            "var",
            "  n: 1..10;",
            "begin",
            "  n := 5;",
            "  n := n * 2;",
            "  writeln(n);",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "10",
            "11",
            "an error",
            "0"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "10 is inside 1..10."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l3-e5",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program stops with a range check error. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "program Dice;",
            "var",
            "  die: 1..6;",
            "begin",
            "  die := 6;",
            "  writeln(die);",
            "  die := die + 1;",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 6,
          "explanation": "7 doesn't fit into 1..6."
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-l3-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why use a subrange instead of a plain integer?",
          "options": [
            "Wrong values are caught right away",
            "It's faster",
            "It uses no memory",
            "It can hold more"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "A month of 13 can't sneak in unnoticed."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}